WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.070
<b>Super Cool Space Girl</b>

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.400
Shirobori Middle School

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.580
Wow!

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:46.820
All right, switch!

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:51.670
Your tennis club skills 
are definitely showing, Misuzu.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.740
A normal middle-schooler wouldn't 
have been able to get that.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.420
That was an average volley for someone 
who's played tennis for twelve months.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:01.960
What the heck? That's hilarious, Misuzu.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:10.680
Hey, those guys keep staring 
at Misuzu. Those pervs.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:18.010
Do you know Kokonose-kun, Misuzu?

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.110
Why do you ask?

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.360
Your eyes just met.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.410
I was just looking at him,

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.990
hoping he'd disappear without a trace.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.370
What the heck?

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.470
Is she laughing at me?

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.300
That's really annoying...

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.370
Misuzu Sonokata? Why...

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.920
She's also an employee here.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.310
I had her observing you for a while.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:50.170
She's... She was observing me?

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.720
Chief, I'm still against this.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:58.210
As I reported earlier, he is 
not qualified to be a police officer.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.750
Yes, well...

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.800
The reason he was talking to himself 
ended up being because of a Monitalien.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.450
He wasn't suffering from delusions after all.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.610
No. There is a much more 
pressing problem at hand.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:08.560
Above all...

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.220
Chuta Kokonose is a pervert.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.630
He is extremely perverted.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.190
I suspect that his daily life is 
filled with perversion.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:19.050
And it is not something slightly endearing
 that will end once he hits puberty—

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:24.960
Well, anyway, do your best, 
just like Misuzu and Chips in Division 2.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.470
Right...

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.670
To think that Sonokata was also 
a member of the Space Police...

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:34.700
Isn't it great? Girl's tennis.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:35.620
Tateyan?

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:38.180
I wanna go over there, too.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:42.120
<i>He doesn't remember what 
happened back then...</i>

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:48.880
<i>Come to think of it, everything that 
happened yesterday was unbelievable.</i>

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.800
<i>Wait, I think I'm forgetting about 
the most unbelievable thing...</i>

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.160
Misuzu hates you, Chuta.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.460
There it is! That weird thing!

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.970
What's wrong, Chuta? 
Are you talking to yourself again?

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:01.560
Huh?

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.000
Oh, y-y-y-y-yeah!

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.710
It's nothing, so don't worry about it.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:06.510
It's heading your way!

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.750
Hey, are you okay, Chuta?

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.980
I'm going to head out for a bit,

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.990
but make sure you get some rest.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.070
Yes, ma'am...

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:27.760
She left.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:28.730
Yeah, she did.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.670
You're still stuck to me?

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.890
Apparently I was exhausted and fell asleep.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:39.040
Materializing into this form uses 
an unimaginable amount of energy.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:40.980
What are you talking about?!

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.620
To think that the voice belonged 
to something as weird as you!

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.500
What the heck are you, anyway?

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.540
A fourth generation Monitalien.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:51.270
<b>Fourth Generation Monitalien. 
Water Planet Support-Type Dolughbritt Type 390</b>

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:51.290
A water planet support-type 
Dolughbritt type 390.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.590
Your name is too long! 
Dolugh should be enough.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.470
Dolugh?!

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.350
Dolugh! Dol-Dol-Dol-Dolugh!

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:03.680
Dolugh!

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.080
I like it.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.160
Come to think of it...

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.330
That embarrassing failure back then...

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.450
That embarrassing experience that one time...

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:16.660
It's all your fault! Give me back my youth!

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:19.900
Age-wise, your youth is just beginning.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.140
Don't lecture me about that! Just get out!

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.320
I wouldn't do that, Chuta.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.510
I can't breathe...

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:32.880
You and I are one. If I'm suffering, 
you will suffer, too.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.020
Then how am I supposed to pull you out?!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.860
You can't pull me out unless you die.

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:39.550
No!

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.760
Then I have to live like this forever?

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.070
I don't need anything other than
my wiener growing from me!

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:52.070
Did she hear me? Or am I safe?

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:55.150
Such vulgar language. 
You really are a pervert.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:57.370
She did hear me!

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.100
We need to go to our night shift.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.120
Huh? You mean for ēlDLIVE?

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:05.000
What else is there? Or would you rather quit?

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.970
Huh? I... I can quit?

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:12.330
Of course. You can run away with your tail 
between your legs and not leave a trace.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:16.470
Actually, you should build up 
the courage to completely disappear.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:19.430
Don't give me that!

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:22.440
N-Not to mention, we have classes right now.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.360
Even if I were the president,
 I would show up

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.990
for my shift at ēlDLIVE, 
even if it meant missing a summit.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:30.490
That's not very easy to understand.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.350
You lack comprehension skills.

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:37.810
Very well. I will tell the chief that you 
can't make it because of classes.

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:38.580
Wha...

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.550
She's so annoying.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.290
Aren't you going after Misuzu, Chuta?

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:48.220
Whoa! Don't suddenly jump out like that!

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.390
We're going to be late for ēlDLIVE! 
We're going to be late on our first day.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.930
Hang on, Dolugh. Why do you 
want to go that badly?

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:56.190
I'm curious.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.050
Huh?

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:00.200
Monitaliens were created 
to gather information.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.940
We are made with a strong 
sense of curiosity.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:03.680
What does that have to do with me?

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.950
You're not going, Chuta?

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:11.190
I don't really understand the Space Police,

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:15.760
but I don't like Sonokata 
mocking me like that.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:22.070
Not to mention, why is it a night shift?

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:23.810
It's still the middle of the day.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.750
Yesterday, it was dark out in space.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:30.490
Maybe space's day and night
 are the opposite of Earth's.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.300
True...

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.740
Huh? Where did Sonokata go? 
I thought she was around here...

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.550
Over here, chu.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:46.930
I'm Inspector Chips, chu! 
Hurry up and get in, chu!

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:49.670
Where are we?

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:51.940
One of ēlDLIVE's Earth branches.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.370
There's, like, nothing here.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:59.680
It's only here so we can transfer to 
the station without getting detected.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.370
More importantly, are you truly 
going to show up for your shift?

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.780
Well, y-yeah!

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.120
All right, here we go, chu!

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:11.220
Changes in the target's particles confirmed.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.860
Please go ahead with the transfer, chu!

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:14.040
Leave it to me, shero.

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:20.460
We were upside down again, chu.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:23.590
Come on, Transfer Administrator Sheronimo.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.750
Huh? It's pretty quiet today.

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:31.390
The daytime staff is off right now, chu.

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:34.190
I see. So that's why it's the night shift...

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:38.340
I've been waiting...

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:39.290
You guys.

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:41.910
Huh? Chief Laine?

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:43.450
Yeah.

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:47.500
Chuta Kokonose and the Monitalien...

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.340
Um... uh...

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:00.340
Chief, no!

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:02.260
You can't sleep here, chu!

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:03.680
When did he fall asleep?

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:07.480
Chips, stand by on the bridge.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.510
Misuzu, give Chuta a tour of the bureau.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.770
Yoyosa!

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:12.770
Yoyosa...

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.670
Space Police ēlDLIVE.

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:19.880
Their bureau in this Solar System 
is this spaceship, the <i>Jeanrenoi-R</i>.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:23.720
This ship is equipped with advanced technologies 
that the ēl Civilization has to offer,

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:25.990
which we on Earth will eventually 
come to grasp ourselves.

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:27.740
I... I see...

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:31.480
There are virus-like translation chips 
operating onboard the ship

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:35.080
and once you breathe them in, 
you are able to talk to all of the aliens here.

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:39.670
This is the sick bay. 
Dr. Isaac is in charge here.

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:41.380
Hi...

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:46.550
That's the transfer operations room.  
This is Second Class Officer Sheronimo.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.020
Nice to meet you, shero.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.880
So that's the transfer guy...

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:52.110
This is the interrogation room.

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:55.110
And this is the SPH research office.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.400
SP... What?

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.620
And this is where we're assigned...

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:04.290
The investigations department.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.390
There are six divisions in 
the investigations department.

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:11.750
You, I, and Investigator Chips 
are assigned to Division 2.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:16.070
Which means there are a lot more 
people besides you and Chips?

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:18.940
Twenty people work in the
 investigations department.

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:19.880
That many?

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:23.140
Our boss at Division 2 
is Section Chief Madigan.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.880
He rarely shows his face,

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.860
but when he does, it'd be 
in your best interest to run.

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.100
What the heck?!

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:32.270
And this is the detention center.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:33.100
So it's like the jail?

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:38.450
A temporary one. The Chabrolian 
you captured earlier is in here.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.130
Huh?

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:45.280
Oh, you're right. 
It's the former Saotome-sensei...

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:49.950
Um, so do vicious criminals
get the death penalty?

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:52.740
Intergalactic law prioritizes rehabilitation.

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:55.540
In most cases, criminals are 
sent to a rehabilitation center.

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:58.800
Wow, so even criminals get a second chance.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.040
That's a nice system.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:03.430
What would you know?

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:04.460
Huh?

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:11.370
Um...

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:15.680
Um...

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.600
Misuzu's mad.

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:22.610
Um... do you mind if I look around 
the bureau by myself a bit?

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:31.620
This place is pretty huge.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.820
Misuzu was in a bad mood.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:38.550
Well, Sonokata always seems
 to be mad at me.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:41.330
And you seem to get angry easily 
when Misuzu's concerned.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:46.700
I don't know why, but whenever I talk 
to Sonokata, I get really annoyed.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:52.970
Maybe... it's because I thought Sonokata 
was cute at first, so when she says mean things...

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:54.000
Chuta.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.540
Where are we?

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:59.100
Where? We're in the...

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:00.770
Wait a sec...

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:03.440
Are we lost?!

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:20.960
<b>Misuzu Sonokata</b>

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.290
Huh? This isn't good...

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.460
This is just going to make 
Sonokata complain again.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:30.210
This is a Code 7! This is a Code 7!

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:32.260
Did I end up someplace weird?

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:32.890
A suspect has escaped 
from the detention center!

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:34.010
Escaped?!

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:39.550
Stop!

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:47.910
Huh? Wha? What should I do?

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:50.490
I repeat, an escaped suspect 
is headed toward B43!

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:50.490
Sonokata!

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.490
That's where Transfer Room 2 is.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:56.160
Second Class Officer Sheronimo.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:13:01.450
I'm sorry... The one that escaped 
is the vicious criminal, Dragline.

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:05.290
He transferred himself, shero. 
He was headed toward Earth, shero.

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.020
To Earth?

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:07.920
I'll go after him.

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.300
G-Go after him?

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:11.970
<b>Matcha</b>

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:11.960
I'm the only one available right now.

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:14.810
Is the transfer unit still operational?

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.560
I'll give it a try, shero.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:19.500
You're not gonna go, Chuta?

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.520
Well, he's a vicious criminal, right?

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:23.770
Misuzu's going, but you're not going to go?

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:27.830
Well... I guess I can 
at least find a criminal...

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:31.650
I'm sure the other officers
 will come save us in a little while.

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:34.400
Please don't come 
if you're going to be so naïve.

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:36.040
It's like you're a middle schooler.

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:39.710
Wha— Of course! I am a middle schooler!

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.580
If you will, Second Class Officer Sheronimo.

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:43.340
Leave it to me, shero.

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:45.000
Hey, wait a sec!

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.010
Transfer!

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:47.960
Ow!

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:52.480
We're upside down again! 
"Leave it to me, shero," my ass...

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:54.090
Um, where are we?

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:56.150
Near the local branch.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:59.430
Apparently he didn't change the coordinates 
from when we headed to the bureau.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:01.640
I wonder where he went...

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:04.280
The alien from Rosenber, Dragline,

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:08.100
was arrested after committing 
three indiscriminate murders.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.160
Indiscriminate murders?!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.450
So he's headed to the 
 crowded shopping district?

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:13.240
No.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:18.370
Considering his situation, 
the first thing he'd probably think of...

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:22.280
Whoa, the local branch!

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:25.750
...is to take care of any pursuing officers.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:27.790
Escapee located.

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:35.130
It looks like a crab, Chuta.

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:37.260
So gross!

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:43.900
This is ēlDLIVE. Do not try to resist,
 and come quietly.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:47.750
I don't think he's going to listen!

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:49.280
Let's catch him, Chuta.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:51.070
We can't catch that thing!

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:54.320
Sonokata!

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:58.200
You have the right to remain silent 
and the right to an attorney.

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:04.250
And...

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:08.660
Anything you say can and will be used 
against you in an intergalactic court of law.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:17.710
Screw your court of law! 
I'm going to kill all I want!

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.470
Do you plan on resisting?

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:22.980
SPH!

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:26.960
He ran away?

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:29.140
He just hiding.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:33.230
I-I'm gonna get killed fighting 
a monster like that unarmed.

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:37.280
I'm here! We arrested that Blob-Blob 
together yesterday, didn't we?

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:40.400
Yesterday was just a coincidence! 
I can't do this.

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.640
So you're just gonna go back 
to being a pessimist, Chuta?

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:47.980
Yesterday, you affirmed yourself, 
and awakened my powers.

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:51.420
I thought you'd regained your confidence
 and accepted your past.

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:58.140
There's no way I can change that easily.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:01.890
Not to mention, it's partially your fault 
that I ended up like this!

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:05.140
It's your fault that I ended up saying 
"wiener" in front of Sonokata today.

00:16:05.570 --> 00:16:07.700
Please stop saying such vulgar things.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:11.900
Oh, right... Sonokata 
can't hear Dolugh's voice.

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:14.520
But you've made things very clear.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:15.440
Huh?

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:21.540
If you can't fight this vicious criminal, 
you are not fit to be in ēlDLIVE.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.710
Please resign without leaving a trace.

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:39.470
Chuta! An old lady and some dogs 
are coming closer.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.010
Hey, what's wrong?

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:47.770
First, I'll get that old hag...

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:50.390
A m-m-monster!

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:57.150
Nice, Chuta!

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:59.030
I... I did that without thinking...

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.330
It's coming, Chuta!

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:04.160
Dolugh, let's sew him up!

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:06.070
Sympathy!

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:12.420
He deflected it? No way...

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:16.530
Are you messing around?

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.000
Dolugh!

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:37.200
Escaping, repeatedly resisting, and...

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:41.110
...attacking civilians.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:45.720
Confirming that apprehending 
the suspect is proving difficult.

00:17:45.720 --> 00:17:49.160
I will perform my duty 
according to regulations.

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.460
Huh? S-Sonokata?

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:56.210
This smell... It's the nice smell from class.

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:20.980
Here I go.

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:24.820
Die, ēlDLIVE!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.360
Please disappear, without a trace.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.520
I was in awe...

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:03.190
But... Does this mean that 
you killed the criminal?

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:04.360
Of course.

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:07.650
He ignored my warnings and attacked.

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:12.580
Misuzu sounds prickly.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:15.240
More like she's super prickly.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:18.050
We're both middle schoolers, but...

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:20.060
...it's like Misuzu Sonokata is...

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.620
....a super cool space girl.

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:33.770
You okay, Misuzu?

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:35.060
Yes.

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:38.900
Eliminating an escaped criminal... 
You sure didn't hold back, did you?

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.340
Thank you for your hard work.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:44.570
There is an Earthling who saw the battle, 
so please take the necessary measures.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.460
Yoyosa!

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:49.780
Oh, so you must be the rookie Earthling.

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:51.110
Huh? Me?

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:54.250
He's no longer a rookie with us.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.590
Apparently, he wants 
nothing to do with ēlDLIVE.

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:57.840
Huh?

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:04.140
Thank you so much. I don't know what 
they would have done if I had died.

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:05.510
You're the old lady from earlier...

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:08.930
It's all because you shielded me.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:10.510
Huh? Me?

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:13.380
Yes. You saved my life.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.770
Thank you so much.

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:19.760
I-It was nothing...

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:25.900
That must have been an ordeal, ma'am.

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:28.460
Please come this way.

00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:36.230
Looks like you've accepted 
yourself a little more.

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:37.120
Huh?

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:42.600
At the same time, you're accepting 
my existence, so I can tell.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:44.920
You're already completely different 
from two days ago, Chuta.

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:49.100
I don't plan on accepting you, Dolugh.

00:20:56.890 --> 00:20:57.890
<i>But...</i>

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:02.250
<i>It's been a while since I felt like this...</i>

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:08.460
I have to complete my report, 
so I'm returning to the bureau.

00:21:08.460 --> 00:21:10.850
You can return to the school if you'd like.

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:13.750
You're quitting, anyway.

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:17.210
Hold on a sec! I never said 
I was going to quit!

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:21.130
And...

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:25.120
If I'm going to quit, 
I'll tell the chief myself!

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:36.920
You sure ended up at a pretty 
gruesome scene from the get-go.

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:39.100
Please use this to wipe 
the blood from your face.

00:21:39.100 --> 00:21:40.090
Blood?

00:21:42.830 --> 00:21:44.210
Green?

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:46.820
B-B-B-B-B....

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:48.950
Blood!

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:54.490
<i>I think I'm going to have to exclude crab 
from my favorite foods for a while...</i>

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:27.770
Hey, Super Cool Space Girl.

00:23:27.770 --> 00:23:30.130
Great job, Super Cool Space Girl.

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:34.040
Officer Kokonose, because of you, 
I ended up with a strange nickname.

00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:35.060
S-Sorry...

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:36.480
Next time on <i>ēlDLIVE,</i>

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Next Time
After the Shoplifter!</b>

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:37.840
"After the Shoplifter!"

00:23:37.840 --> 00:23:39.920
Please disappear, without a trace.
